  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This paper estimates county-level daily consumption levels across China using Baidu Population Profiling data to analyze nationwide spatial variation and driver mechanisms. High consumption levels concentrate heavily in eastern coastal urban agglomerations, with administrative status and local urbanization rates driving regional disparities. Improved commercial markets reduce the proportion of low-level consumers, whereas enhanced consumption amenities correlate more strongly with growing the high-level consumer population.",
      "why": "It moves Chinese consumption research past coarse regional aggregates and localized municipal studies, mapping daily expenditure structures down to county administrative units nationwide."
